      <div type="clause" n="49.7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 49.7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 49.7" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="572" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si placitum sit furti uel exaccionis huiusmodi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="50" target="#Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.50"/>, et unus inculpatorum adducatur ad reddendum quod exigitur, non reddent alii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="m" target="#Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.m"/>: quia ex una<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="n" target="#Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.n"/> culpa non debent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="51" target="#Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.51"/> in hunc modum plures emendaciones haberi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="52" target="#Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.52"/>. Debet autem de conuictis iusticia fieri.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 572 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.m" n="m" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">572</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">für Einen Diebstahl Mehrerer erhält Kläger einmal Ersatz; Leibesstrafe aber erleiden alle überführten Mitthäter grösseren Diebstahls; ebenso</hi> 59, 25</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">for one theft committed by several persons the plaintiff receives restitution once; but all the convicted accomplices in a greater theft suffer corporal punishment; likewise 59, 25</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.n" n="n" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">572</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 94, 1<hi rend="italic">b</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 94, 1b</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.50" n="50" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">572</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eiusm. <hi rend="italic">Lond,</hi> huius <hi rend="italic">Wh</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eiusm. Lond, huius Wh</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.51" n="51" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">572</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">debet <hi rend="italic">K Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">debet K Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.52" n="52" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">572</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-re <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-re Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_49-7.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die nur zu Geldzahlungen (Ersatz samt Busse und an den Richter Strafe) führende <hi rend="italic">actio</hi> steht in Ggs. zu der mit Leibesstrafe zu ahnenden Überführtheit letzter Zeile, die nur anderes Wort für handhaft (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1g) sein muss.—<hi rend="italic">eiusmodi</hi>{50} Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The <hi rend="italic">actio</hi>, which leads only to money payments (restitution together with compensation, and a fine to the judge), stands in contrast to the conviction in the last line, to be punished with corporal punishment, which must simply be another word for ‘caught in the act’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1g).—<hi rend="italic">eiusmodi</hi>{50} Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
